The 1914–15 Scottish football season was [[Celtic F.C.|Celtic]]'s 27th season of competitive football, in which they competed in the [[Scottish First Division]].<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.londonhearts.com/scores/a1910/celtic1915.htm|title=Results for Celtic for 1914-15|website=www.londonhearts.com|access-date=19 June 2018|archive-date=23 June 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180623005146/http://www.londonhearts.com/scores/a1910/celtic1915.htm|url-status=live}}</ref> They retained their League title as they ended up with 65 points, four ahead of runners-up [[Heart of Midlothian F.C.|Hearts]].

The [[Scottish Cup]], which Celtic held as champions, was not played this season because of World War I.

Celtic won the [[Glasgow Charity Cup|Glasgow Merchants' Charity Cup]] for the fourth year in a row.

The season was capped up with a charity fundraising match against a Scottish League XI made of players from the rest of the league at [[Hampden Park]], which Celtic won 1-0.

